,"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the stored exact per-platform release URL the sole source of the gitleaks asset name (do not reconstruct it from the `amd64`/`arm64` platform key), acknowledging the gitleaks `linux_x64` vs `amd64` naming difference.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Dockerfile.reviewbot:52-53: `arm64) gl_arch=arm64 ;; amd64) gl_arch=x64 ;;` — the gitleaks amd64 asset is `gitleaks_${ver}_linux_x64.tar.gz`","Plan keys entries on `linux/amd64`/`linux/arm64`","EVIDENCE CLASS: Verified (repo code confirms the asset arch-naming mismatch)"],"finding":"The provisioning helper is said to 'select the manifest entry from Docker's target OS/architecture', but Gitleaks release assets label the x86-64 build `linux_x64` (not `amd64`) per the existing Dockerfile arch map, so an OS/arch-derived URL requires an amd64->x64 translation the plan does not call out.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f49f42c4dc6f468d7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: 'selects the manifest entry from Docker’s target OS/architecture or the CI runner’s actual OS/architecture'","norm_id":"nf2c2396fc92a8717","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A helper that derives the download URL from the platform key `amd64` instead of reading the stored exact URL would request a nonexistent `linux_amd64` asset (404)"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that the helper resolves the download URL by reading the manifest entry's exact `url` field verbatim, using the OS/arch only to pick the entry.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_